`lib/Pod/Weaver/PluginBundle/Author/GETTY.pm` (COMMANDS, lines 76-131) documents ten custom commands. `lib/Pod/Elemental/Transformer/Author/GETTY.pm:43-58` implements `synopsis`, `description`, `seealso` (head1) and `attr method func opt env hook example` (head2). Differences:

- `=resource` (documented line 76) and `=event` (line 100) are in neither table. They pass through untouched and end up as unknown POD commands in the built module, which is a POD error on MetaCPAN.
- `=seealso L<Some::Other::Module>` (line 129): the transformer replaces the whole command line with the fixed heading `SEE ALSO` (`Transformer:70-73`), so the link written on the command line is dropped without a word. Only the paragraphs below it survive.
- The other way round, `=synopsis` and `=description` work but are documented only in the transformer, not in the bundle's COMMANDS list.

No fleet dist uses `=resource`, `=event` or a `=seealso` with content today (grep over `p5-*/lib`), so nothing is broken yet; the docs just promise more than there is.

Done when docs and tables agree: either add `resource` and `event` to `@HEAD2_COMMANDS` with a test, or remove them from the POD; and document `=seealso` as taking no argument.

